From: NightHammer1000 <nightstorm@kpc.bz>
Date: Sat, 4 Apr 2026 17:15:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tu: expose Vulkan 1.4 on a6xx

Upstream gates Vulkan 1.4 on `pdevice->info->chip >= 7` and reports 1.3 for
Adreno 6xx. Expose TU_API_VERSION regardless of the chip generation.

Everything Vulkan 1.4 raises beyond 1.3 is met by turnip except
maxBoundDescriptorSets, which a6xx reports as 4 where 1.4 requires 7: a6xx
has 5 bindless bases and reserves one for the driver, so there is no spare
descriptor set. A driver built with this patch is therefore not conformant,
and an application that allocates seven descriptor sets because 1.4 promises
seven will fail on a6xx. The other raised limits are met: image dimensions
16384/16384/2048/16384 against 8192/8192/512/8192, maxImageArrayLayers 2048
against 2048, maxUniformBufferRange 65536 against 65536, maxPushConstantsSize
256 against 256.

Signed-off-by: NightHammer1000 <nightstorm@kpc.bz>
---
diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
index e8ef940..30d0e0b 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
@@ -1295,8 +1295,7 @@ tu_get_properties(struct tu_physical_device *pdevice,
 
    props->apiVersion =
       tu_has_multiview(pdevice) ?
-         ((pdevice->info->chip >= 7) ? TU_API_VERSION :
-            VK_MAKE_VERSION(1, 3, VK_HEADER_VERSION))
+         TU_API_VERSION
          : VK_MAKE_VERSION(1, 0, VK_HEADER_VERSION);
    props->driverVersion = vk_get_driver_version();
    props->vendorID = pdevice->instance->drirc.debug.force_vk_vendor != 0 ?
